1
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:48,950
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:51,800
[Episode 4]

3
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:04,200
Morning, Angel's Tears.

4
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:06,920
Morning, Scythe.

5
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:09,680
Still a fan of Han Geng?

6
00:02:09,910 --> 00:02:11,680
If you ask me, you should be my fan.

7
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:14,140
I look so handsome
when playing basketball.

8
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:16,150
Don't even bring it up.
Just thinking about it ticks me off.

9
00:02:16,150 --> 00:02:18,150
My mom doesn't even
let me go online anymore.

10
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:19,430
I've had it good these past few days.

11
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:20,750
My dad's over the moon,

12
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:23,120
all because I'm entering the math contest.

13
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:24,120
The math contest?

14
00:02:24,150 --> 00:02:25,680
Who are you teaming up with?

15
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:27,210
Lin Zhixia and Shen Fuxuan.

16
00:02:28,590 --> 00:02:29,470
Lin Zhixia?

17
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:32,310
Then I'd rather never go online
for the rest of my life.

18
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:33,800
You're dead last in the class.

19
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:34,910
Even if you wanted to join,

20
00:02:34,910 --> 00:02:36,970
you'd need a team willing to take you.

21
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:37,840
I...

22
00:02:40,079 --> 00:02:40,710
Get lost.

23
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:42,960
Fine, I'll go.

24
00:02:43,590 --> 00:02:45,390
Make sure you don't show up late.

25
00:02:47,190 --> 00:02:48,120
Wait for me!

26
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:55,240
The contest is only 10 days away.

27
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:57,079
Based on each of our strengths and needs,

28
00:02:57,079 --> 00:02:58,360
I've put together a study plan.

29
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,150
Take a look.

30
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,000
Okay.

31
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:04,210
If we finish this plan before the contest,

32
00:03:04,210 --> 00:03:05,740
we should be in good shape.

33
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:08,090
Take a look and see
if there's anything else

34
00:03:08,090 --> 00:03:09,750
you think needs improvement.

35
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,150
Lin Zhixia,

36
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:13,530
this is 10 days' worth of work?

37
00:03:17,630 --> 00:03:19,030
I have no problem with it.

38
00:03:29,470 --> 00:03:30,280
Okay.

39
00:03:30,870 --> 00:03:31,680
Okay.

40
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:33,240
Then let's get our things together

41
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,240
and meet at the library.

42
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:34,840
Okay.

43
00:03:37,910 --> 00:03:39,360
I'm going to the restroom.

44
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:41,020
I'll catch up with you in a bit.

45
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:48,300
[A New Chapter, A New Journey]

46
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:54,870
I've got a problem.

47
00:03:56,960 --> 00:04:00,290
Had I known it'd be this exhausting,
I wouldn't have joined.

48
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:07,910
Duan Qiyan,

49
00:04:08,150 --> 00:04:09,610
let me see your study plan.

50
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:19,290
[A New Chapter, A New Journey]

51
00:04:16,870 --> 00:04:18,040
I can't show it to you.

52
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,390
Aren't you our competitor?

53
00:04:19,390 --> 00:04:21,120
It's classified information.

54
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:23,890
[A New Chapter, A New Journey]

55
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:33,360
Alright.

56
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,830
That's it for now.

57
00:04:34,070 --> 00:04:36,540
[Please Keep Quiet in the Library]

58
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:37,140
We'll continue after school.

59
00:04:37,830 --> 00:04:38,220
Okay.

60
00:04:38,390 --> 00:04:40,320
We'll still be going after school?

61
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:42,810
Isn't today's workload a little too much?

62
00:04:42,870 --> 00:04:44,670
Didn't you look at the schedule?

63
00:04:44,830 --> 00:04:46,560
Why are you still complaining?

64
00:04:47,190 --> 00:04:49,430
Actually, your fundamentals aren't bad.

65
00:04:49,430 --> 00:04:51,850
Once you get used to
contest-style thinking,

66
00:04:51,850 --> 00:04:53,659
it won't just help you in this contest—

67
00:04:53,659 --> 00:04:56,260
it'll help with your studies
in the future too.

68
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:57,860
I don't know...

69
00:05:50,570 --> 00:05:51,250
Duan Qiyan.

70
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:54,950
How's your contest prep going?

71
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:59,100
This is no way to live.

72
00:06:00,890 --> 00:06:01,930
I've got an idea

73
00:06:01,930 --> 00:06:04,190
that'll make things a lot easier for you.

74
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:10,300
Tell me more about it.

75
00:06:10,810 --> 00:06:12,810
From what I saw of Lin Zhixia's plan,

76
00:06:12,890 --> 00:06:13,620
her focus

77
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:15,540
is on developing your overall ability.

78
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:18,300
She wants to turn both of you
into versions of herself.

79
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:20,500
However, we want each person
to play to their strengths

80
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:21,890
and work together as a team.

81
00:06:21,890 --> 00:06:22,690
You wouldn't need to study

82
00:06:22,690 --> 00:06:24,290
all that advanced material—

83
00:06:24,330 --> 00:06:27,190
just what's needed
for this contest specifically.

84
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:29,540
So, do you want to join our team?

85
00:06:37,750 --> 00:06:42,409
[Registration Form]

86
00:06:40,330 --> 00:06:41,420
Why is Duan Qiyan's name

87
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:42,680
on both of these forms?

88
00:06:53,490 --> 00:06:54,700
[Registration Form]

89
00:06:58,070 --> 00:06:58,870
Ms. Wu,

90
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:01,500
why don't we just ask Duan Qiyan himself?

91
00:07:07,390 --> 00:07:08,650
I'm sorry, Lin Zhixia.

92
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:12,080
I think I'd be a better fit
on Jin Baihui's team.

93
00:07:12,430 --> 00:07:13,430
I was actually planning

94
00:07:13,430 --> 00:07:14,800
to tell you guys about this today.

95
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:15,560
But I didn't expect

96
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,390
the registration forms
to reach the teacher so fast.

97
00:07:18,390 --> 00:07:20,590
Didn't you already promise Lin Zhixia?

98
00:07:21,830 --> 00:07:22,600
You don't know.

99
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:24,680
Their training is way too intense.

100
00:07:24,830 --> 00:07:26,830
I'm afraid I won't be able to keep up.

101
00:07:28,630 --> 00:07:30,240
Didn't we agree on this before?

102
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:31,700
How can you be so disloyal?

103
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:32,600
Well...

104
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:35,270
This has nothing to do with loyalty.

105
00:07:35,270 --> 00:07:36,000
Before registration closes,

106
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,820
every contestant has the right
to choose whichever team they want.

107
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:38,820
That's not wrong.

108
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:53,159
Alright, that's settled then.

109
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:55,040
There are only 2 days left
until registration closes.

110
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,840
Hurry up and find a new teammate.

111
00:08:18,070 --> 00:08:19,430
That traitor Duan Qiyan,

112
00:08:19,430 --> 00:08:20,510
so unreliable.

113
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:24,680
There are only 2 days left
until registration closes.

114
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:26,430
Where are we supposed to find someone now?

115
00:08:26,430 --> 00:08:27,240
It's okay.

116
00:08:27,870 --> 00:08:29,000
We'll find someone.

117
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:36,909
Duan Qiyan,

118
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:39,840
that was seriously lacking in team spirit.

119
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:41,789
I invited him.

120
00:08:43,890 --> 00:08:44,700
Jiang Yubai,

121
00:08:45,670 --> 00:08:47,800
do you think I'm targeting Lin Zhixia?

122
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,240
You're wrong.

123
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:53,200
I am helping you—helping our team.

124
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:56,120
You only care about defeating Lin Zhixia.

125
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:57,360
But this is a team competition,

126
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:58,690
not your personal show.

127
00:08:59,670 --> 00:09:00,550
But he is Lin Zhixia's

128
00:09:00,550 --> 00:09:01,960
hard-won teammate.

129
00:09:02,790 --> 00:09:03,960
Duan Qiyan is a person,

130
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,080
not some object.

131
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:07,360
If he genuinely wanted to
stay on their team,

132
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:09,690
could I have still
gotten him to join ours?

133
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,270
Besides,

134
00:09:14,630 --> 00:09:16,490
we didn't have a full team before,

135
00:09:16,670 --> 00:09:18,200
and Duan Qiyan is a good fit.

136
00:09:18,390 --> 00:09:19,630
Math modeling contest problems

137
00:09:19,630 --> 00:09:21,360
often involve real-world scenarios.

138
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:22,600
Duan Qiyan is good at physics.

139
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,750
He can quickly identify
the physical principles behind a problem,

140
00:09:24,750 --> 00:09:28,600
helping us avoid going down
unnecessary mathematical rabbit holes.

141
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:31,000
Isn't the whole point of the contest
to win?

142
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:34,000
So who exactly is the one
lacking team spirit here?

143
00:09:36,270 --> 00:09:37,080
I'm sorry.

144
00:09:37,860 --> 00:09:40,460
I let my personal feelings
affect the contest.

145
00:09:41,150 --> 00:09:42,880
But originally, I thought that

146
00:09:43,030 --> 00:09:44,770
if we needed to find a teammate,

147
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:47,970
it'd be much easier for us
than for Lin Zhixia.

148
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:49,120
That's true.

149
00:09:50,150 --> 00:09:51,670
Even someone as easygoing as me

150
00:09:51,670 --> 00:09:52,840
has already come to your team.

151
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:55,360
I figured no one would dare join hers.

152
00:09:55,790 --> 00:09:57,670
Could you just talk a little less?

153
00:10:15,790 --> 00:10:16,510
Let's go.

154
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,870
Attention, students.

155
00:10:25,630 --> 00:10:26,440
This week,

156
00:10:26,670 --> 00:10:29,320
the school will provide
centralized training for those registered

157
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:30,960
for the Star of Hope Math Contest

158
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:33,790
to improve your chances
of passing the preliminary round.

159
00:10:33,790 --> 00:10:35,120
There will also be teams

160
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:38,000
from other schools
competing in the preliminary round.

161
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,320
Students, we cannot let our guard down.

162
00:10:41,150 --> 00:10:42,680
The competition is fierce,

163
00:10:42,910 --> 00:10:45,030
and the elimination rate is high.

164
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:49,910
During the training, the teachers
will move quickly through the lessons,

165
00:10:49,910 --> 00:10:51,270
and there will be a lot of assignments.

166
00:10:51,270 --> 00:10:53,670
Your academic workload will be very heavy.

167
00:10:54,390 --> 00:10:57,000
The lecture hall
will stay open every day at noon,

168
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,030
so you can come here to rest.

169
00:10:57,900 --> 00:11:03,540
[Lin Zhixia; Shen Fuxuan]

170
00:10:59,550 --> 00:11:01,480
Let's push through this together.

171
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,600
And let's aim for good results.

172
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:08,200
Are you confident you can do this?

173
00:11:08,550 --> 00:11:09,320
-Yes.
-Yes.

174
00:11:09,670 --> 00:11:10,270
Good.

175
00:11:10,690 --> 00:11:14,340
[Study Plan: Day 1]

176
00:11:14,410 --> 00:11:15,720
[Past Exam Practice] [Review of Mistakes]

177
00:11:19,130 --> 00:11:19,770
Here.

178
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:27,200
Forget about finding a teammate for now.

179
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:29,800
Want to solve a math problem
to clear your head?

180
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,550
What math problem?

181
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:34,240
One day,

182
00:11:34,630 --> 00:11:36,870
a triangle, a circle, and a square

183
00:11:36,910 --> 00:11:38,510
made plans to go shopping together.

184
00:11:38,510 --> 00:11:40,770
The square and the circle both showed up.

185
00:11:40,910 --> 00:11:42,720
What is this situation called?

186
00:11:44,670 --> 00:11:45,930
This is a math problem?

187
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:52,120
I honestly don't know.

188
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:54,930
What is this situation called?

189
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:58,070
This situation is called

190
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:05,420
"a congruent triangle."
(Chinese pun: "congruent triangle" sounds like "everyone’s waiting for the triangle.")

191
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:12,030
Not funny?

192
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:14,150
It is funny.

193
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:15,850
You're hilarious.

194
00:12:21,510 --> 00:12:23,840
I know you're trying to comfort me.

195
00:12:24,510 --> 00:12:26,270
If only Duan Qiyan hadn't left.

196
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,320
The preliminary round is about to start.

197
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:29,910
Those who plan to participate

198
00:12:29,910 --> 00:12:31,150
already have a team.

199
00:12:31,150 --> 00:12:33,410
It's really not easy to find someone now.

200
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:38,050
Let's eat first.

201
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:46,750
It wasn't me.

202
00:12:46,750 --> 00:12:48,120
If it wasn't you, then who was it?

203
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:49,270
The cabinet door opened by itself?

204
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:50,440
I don't know either.

205
00:12:50,550 --> 00:12:52,030
It was like this when I came back.

206
00:12:52,030 --> 00:12:52,750
Come on,

207
00:12:52,870 --> 00:12:54,550
if you did it, just own up to it.

208
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:55,960
I'm telling the truth.

209
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:57,000
It wasn't me.

210
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,870
Then how come he saw you here?

211
00:12:58,870 --> 00:12:59,550
Who?

212
00:12:59,550 --> 00:13:00,320
Him!

213
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,630
You believe everything he says?

214
00:13:02,630 --> 00:13:04,080
What are you, his lackey?

215
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,790
What's that supposed to mean?

216
00:13:05,790 --> 00:13:06,550
What do I mean?

217
00:13:06,550 --> 00:13:07,630
I'm just stating facts.
What's wrong with that?

218
00:13:07,630 --> 00:13:08,240
You got a problem with that?

219
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:09,120
He was stating the facts too.

220
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:10,200
You were right here.

221
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:12,670
-Didn't I make myself clear?
-What happened?

222
00:13:12,670 --> 00:13:15,200
They said Mr. Wang locked
the test papers for the first round

223
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:16,120
and the answer keys

224
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,650
inside the podium cabinet.

225
00:13:17,750 --> 00:13:19,880
Someone picked the lock at noon today.

226
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:21,440
Not "someone."

227
00:13:21,670 --> 00:13:23,120
It was Duan Qiyan.

228
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,910
Right, it was him.

229
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:27,440
While everyone else was
taking their lunch break,

230
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:29,570
he came here alone and picked the lock.

231
00:13:30,270 --> 00:13:32,360
You say you weren't trying to
steal the answer keys, right?

232
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:33,790
Then at 12:30 PM,

233
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,510
when everyone had gone to eat,

234
00:13:35,510 --> 00:13:36,910
why did you come here by yourself?

235
00:13:36,910 --> 00:13:38,200
Were you really that busy?

236
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:39,960
It's because I brought a USB drive

237
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:42,860
and wanted to copy
the teachers' slides to take home.

238
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:44,650
The computer was in the drawer,
still plugged in.

239
00:13:44,650 --> 00:13:46,440
Where else was I supposed to do it
but at the podium?

240
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:47,480
Who can prove it?

241
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:48,610
Exactly.

242
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:50,540
Who among you can prove it?

243
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:53,270
This is the teammate
you went to such great lengths

244
00:13:53,270 --> 00:13:54,200
to recruit.

245
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:57,770
Shouldn't you show some team spirit
and help him out?

246
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,750
But Duan Qiyan's grades

247
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,530
are better than most people's.

248
00:14:05,050 --> 00:14:06,490
Why would he steal the answer keys?

249
00:14:06,490 --> 00:14:07,080
Exactly.

250
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:08,960
Did you hear that?

251
00:14:09,010 --> 00:14:10,530
Why would I need to steal the answer keys?

252
00:14:10,530 --> 00:14:12,410
You're out playing basketball
every single day.

253
00:14:12,410 --> 00:14:13,740
You know better than anyone

254
00:14:13,740 --> 00:14:15,170
where you actually stand academically.

255
00:14:15,170 --> 00:14:16,500
If you didn't steal the answer keys,

256
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:18,700
how else could your grades be this good?

257
00:14:21,050 --> 00:14:23,580
Duan Qiyan, can I take a look
at your USB drive?

258
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:39,960
When you were copying the files,

259
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,390
was the cabinet still intact?

260
00:14:41,390 --> 00:14:43,390
Yes. I remember that very clearly,

261
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,510
because I started copying the files

262
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:46,570
at around 12:30 PM.

263
00:14:46,650 --> 00:14:48,250
It only took about 2 minutes.

264
00:14:49,030 --> 00:14:52,230
The more details you give,
the more suspicious you sound.

265
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:56,170
You didn't just memorize
the exact time on purpose, did you?

266
00:14:56,790 --> 00:14:58,630
Kuang Geng, what are you implying?

267
00:14:58,630 --> 00:15:02,120
-You don't know what I mean?
-What do you mean? Wanna pick a fight?

268
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:03,650
Isn't he just trying to stir up trouble?

269
00:15:03,650 --> 00:15:06,180
When was the cabinet
discovered to be broken?

270
00:15:06,250 --> 00:15:07,410
And who found it?

271
00:15:07,530 --> 00:15:08,370
I found it.

272
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:10,170
I'd just finished lunch,

273
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:11,580
around 12:50 PM,

274
00:15:11,980 --> 00:15:14,980
and when I came in,
the door was already open like that.

275
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:16,890
After copying the files,

276
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:18,820
I went to the cafeteria
to grab a chicken burger

277
00:15:18,820 --> 00:15:20,530
and planned to bring it back here to eat.

278
00:15:20,530 --> 00:15:21,500
You and I—

279
00:15:21,530 --> 00:15:23,590
we went back here one after the other.

280
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:25,460
How could it possibly have been me?

281
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:27,580
I was napping in this classroom
the whole time.

282
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:29,170
No one came in during that period—

283
00:15:29,170 --> 00:15:29,940
only you.

284
00:15:30,770 --> 00:15:32,830
You were napping here the whole time?

285
00:15:33,170 --> 00:15:33,980
Yeah.

286
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:35,360
In that case...

287
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:38,360
there are very few witnesses.

288
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:41,490
Your statement is crucial.

289
00:15:41,770 --> 00:15:44,300
You need to think carefully
before you speak.

290
00:15:45,750 --> 00:15:47,320
A real man owns up to what he does.

291
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:48,700
If I'd done this, I'd definitely admit it.

292
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:49,750
But I really didn't do it.

293
00:15:49,750 --> 00:15:51,410
Quit making things up about me.

294
00:15:51,410 --> 00:15:52,070
Who's making things up?

295
00:15:52,070 --> 00:15:52,850
Who's making things up?

296
00:15:52,850 --> 00:15:54,120
-How are we making anything up?
-I said you two.

297
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,120
I haven't even...

298
00:16:03,250 --> 00:16:04,310
What are you doing?

299
00:16:04,870 --> 00:16:05,800
Starting a riot?

300
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:16,270
Who opened the cabinet?

301
00:16:17,370 --> 00:16:18,170
Sir,

302
00:16:18,810 --> 00:16:19,350
he did.

303
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:22,300
Seriously, Liu Su?
Are you ever going to stop?

304
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:30,960
Hey, you dropped this.

305
00:16:32,110 --> 00:16:33,010
It's not mine.

306
00:16:34,690 --> 00:16:36,250
If I'd really picked that lock,

307
00:16:36,250 --> 00:16:37,500
I'd have taken the exam papers out

308
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:38,250
and smashed you over the head with them—

309
00:16:38,250 --> 00:16:39,690
then you'd finally come in first place!

310
00:16:39,690 --> 00:16:40,530
Smash me then!

311
00:16:40,860 --> 00:16:42,890
Stop it! Both of you!

312
00:16:43,340 --> 00:16:45,860
Mr. Wang, Duan Qiyan is innocent.

313
00:16:47,050 --> 00:16:48,100
I checked the timestamp

314
00:16:48,100 --> 00:16:49,700
of the files on his USB drive.

315
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:52,370
They were transferred at exactly 12:37 PM.

316
00:16:52,370 --> 00:16:53,580
What does that prove?

317
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:55,420
He could've copied the files

318
00:16:55,530 --> 00:16:56,880
and looked at the answer keys
at the same time.

319
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:57,960
Besides,

320
00:16:57,980 --> 00:16:59,510
Kuang Geng already saw him.

321
00:16:59,750 --> 00:17:01,210
Let's make an assumption.

322
00:17:01,670 --> 00:17:03,440
If you were Duan Qiyan,

323
00:17:04,109 --> 00:17:06,710
what would you do first—
look at the answer keys

324
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:08,270
or copy the files?

325
00:17:10,510 --> 00:17:11,839
If it were me,

326
00:17:12,069 --> 00:17:14,069
I'd take advantage of the empty room

327
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,000
and read through the answer keys first.

328
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:16,829
That way,

329
00:17:17,069 --> 00:17:20,000
I'd also copy the files afterward
to cover my tracks.

330
00:17:20,069 --> 00:17:21,000
Right now, there are files

331
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:22,460
on Duan Qiyan's USB drive.

332
00:17:22,589 --> 00:17:24,310
If he really were the culprit,

333
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:26,310
that would mean
he would've already calmly read

334
00:17:26,310 --> 00:17:27,400
the answer keys in secret,

335
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:29,930
then covered his tracks
by copying the files.

336
00:17:30,270 --> 00:17:31,720
But the actual scene right now

337
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:33,200
looks like a complete mess—

338
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:34,720
which shows that the culprit

339
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,400
fled in a panic.

340
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:38,380
Duan Qiyan isn't the culprit.

341
00:17:38,550 --> 00:17:39,350
Impossible.

342
00:17:39,830 --> 00:17:41,030
That whole analysis of yours

343
00:17:41,030 --> 00:17:42,510
is just speculation.

344
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,110
Kuang Geng,

345
00:17:44,310 --> 00:17:46,830
I remember you said
that during the lunch break,

346
00:17:46,830 --> 00:17:49,200
only Duan Qiyan came back, right?

347
00:17:49,740 --> 00:17:50,530
Right.

348
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:53,940
Then this problem becomes very simple.

349
00:17:54,090 --> 00:17:55,890
If Duan Qiyan isn't the culprit,

350
00:17:56,940 --> 00:17:58,670
then it must be you, Kuang Geng.

351
00:17:58,900 --> 00:18:01,080
You're slandering me
with baseless accusations!

352
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,770
I was napping at the time.

353
00:18:03,030 --> 00:18:04,900
Maybe someone else came in...

354
00:18:05,010 --> 00:18:06,430
At noon today,

355
00:18:06,490 --> 00:18:07,900
I saw a paper clip

356
00:18:07,900 --> 00:18:09,450
fall out of your pants pocket.

357
00:18:09,450 --> 00:18:10,610
I picked it up and gave it back to you,

358
00:18:10,610 --> 00:18:11,970
but you denied it was yours.

359
00:18:11,970 --> 00:18:13,970
I thought it was strange at the time—

360
00:18:14,050 --> 00:18:15,420
why did you refuse to admit

361
00:18:15,420 --> 00:18:16,370
it was yours?

362
00:18:18,310 --> 00:18:20,110
Let's make another assumption.

363
00:18:20,110 --> 00:18:23,180
Before lunch today, Kuang Geng had already

364
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:25,480
planned to use a paper clip
to pick the lock

365
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:26,940
and steal the answer keys.

366
00:18:27,590 --> 00:18:29,480
Finally, lunch break arrived.

367
00:18:29,550 --> 00:18:31,240
Everyone left the classroom,

368
00:18:31,310 --> 00:18:32,960
and you got your chance.

369
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:35,560
But at that exact moment,

370
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:37,360
Duan Qiyan came back.

371
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:43,640
So you could only pretend to nap.

372
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,590
After Duan Qiyan left,

373
00:18:45,830 --> 00:18:48,310
you took out the paper clip
you'd prepared beforehand,

374
00:18:48,310 --> 00:18:51,440
picked the lock,
and started looking at the answer keys.

375
00:18:55,510 --> 00:18:56,400
Halfway through,

376
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:58,960
you heard the sound of students
coming back toward the classroom,

377
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:01,680
so you hastily put the answer keys back.

378
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:03,700
Whatever the result,

379
00:19:03,770 --> 00:19:05,270
let's leave it in fate's hands.

380
00:19:05,270 --> 00:19:07,200
You fled in a rush
without even having time

381
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:08,550
to clean up the scene.

382
00:19:09,070 --> 00:19:10,270
Another assumption?

383
00:19:10,350 --> 00:19:11,790
How do you come up with so much nonsense?

384
00:19:11,790 --> 00:19:12,880
I'm warning you—

385
00:19:13,030 --> 00:19:15,110
without solid evidence, you should also

386
00:19:15,110 --> 00:19:16,770
be careful about what you say.

387
00:19:17,110 --> 00:19:18,750
The lock cylinder has diagonal scratches,

388
00:19:18,750 --> 00:19:21,000
deeper on the left
and shallower on the right,

389
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,260
which shows the culprit is left-handed.

390
00:19:24,070 --> 00:19:25,330
And in this classroom,

391
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:28,000
only Kuang Geng is left-handed.

392
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:30,080
How did you know that?

393
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:32,510
Everyone, you can check the positions

394
00:19:32,510 --> 00:19:34,640
of the books and water cups on the desks.

395
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:36,160
Everyone else has theirs placed
on the right;

396
00:19:36,160 --> 00:19:38,110
only Kuang Geng has his on the left.

397
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,200
Also, because we write frequently,

398
00:19:41,350 --> 00:19:42,920
we wear our watches

399
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:44,880
on our non-dominant wrist.

400
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:47,900
Everyone, you can check
Kuang Geng's watch.

401
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:50,200
He's wearing it on his right wrist.

402
00:19:54,590 --> 00:19:55,960
I also noticed just now

403
00:19:56,030 --> 00:19:58,110
that there's a tiny blue mark
on the lock cylinder.

404
00:19:58,110 --> 00:20:01,240
It should be from the coating
on the paper clip peeling off.

405
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:02,750
Given how little time you had,

406
00:20:02,750 --> 00:20:05,750
you probably weren't able to
get rid of the paper clip.

407
00:20:05,750 --> 00:20:06,780
So I guess

408
00:20:06,830 --> 00:20:08,480
the paper clip you used to pick the lock

409
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:09,810
is still in your pocket.

410
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:20,640
Mr. Wang, look.

411
00:20:31,550 --> 00:20:32,350
Zhixia,

412
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:35,790
you stayed calm earlier,
thought things through logically,

413
00:20:35,790 --> 00:20:37,880
and exposed the person
who was really cheating.

414
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:39,140
That deserves praise.

415
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:43,930
However, I still have to
call you out on one thing:

416
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,660
you were a bit reckless today.

417
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:48,680
Why?

418
00:20:50,590 --> 00:20:52,720
You're all in adolescence now.

419
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:55,680
Pride and dignity
matter more than anything.

420
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:57,070
By exposing him in front of everyone,

421
00:20:57,070 --> 00:20:59,600
you've basically
made an enemy, understand?

422
00:21:02,510 --> 00:21:03,400
I understand.

423
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:06,070
But they were falsely accusing Duan Qiyan
at the time.

424
00:21:06,070 --> 00:21:06,920
The situation was urgent,

425
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:08,380
so I didn't think that far.

426
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:09,280
I understand.

427
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:12,700
If something similar happens again,

428
00:21:13,070 --> 00:21:14,870
tell the teacher your reasoning

429
00:21:15,030 --> 00:21:16,690
and let the teacher handle it.

430
00:21:17,960 --> 00:21:20,760
I'm just worried
he might try to get revenge on you.

431
00:21:20,830 --> 00:21:23,090
You're a girl. Who will protect you then?

432
00:21:24,030 --> 00:21:24,640
-Me.
-Me.

433
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:41,680
And me!

434
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,440
From today on,

435
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:46,720
I, Duan Qiyan, swear to protect
Lin Zhixia with my life.

436
00:21:58,240 --> 00:21:59,830
Isn't it a little over the top
for the three of you

437
00:21:59,830 --> 00:22:01,230
to walk me home like this?

438
00:22:02,160 --> 00:22:03,070
Not at all.

439
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:04,510
It's what I should do.

440
00:22:05,070 --> 00:22:07,920
Zhixia, not only did you help me
find my sports player cards,

441
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:09,830
but you also defended my innocence.

442
00:22:09,830 --> 00:22:12,440
I owe you my life for this.

443
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:13,750
So, Zhixia,

444
00:22:13,750 --> 00:22:15,790
if you ever need any help in the future,

445
00:22:15,790 --> 00:22:16,990
tell me immediately.

446
00:22:17,590 --> 00:22:18,560
Duan Qiyan,

447
00:22:18,590 --> 00:22:20,270
your attitude sure did a 180.

448
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:22,530
You have some nerve saying that.

449
00:22:22,530 --> 00:22:23,790
If it weren't for you,

450
00:22:23,910 --> 00:22:25,910
would she have had all this trouble?

451
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:34,200
Zhixia,

452
00:22:34,960 --> 00:22:37,290
I know
your team is still missing a member.

453
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:39,880
But I've already submitted
my contest registration form.

454
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:41,680
Trying to go back to your team now

455
00:22:41,830 --> 00:22:43,360
probably isn't realistic.

456
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:48,700
But if I really can't
find another teammate,

457
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,930
I might not be able to participate.

458
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:57,460
I have someone in mind.

459
00:22:58,770 --> 00:22:59,290
Who?

460
00:23:00,850 --> 00:23:03,440
Mom, don't force me to participate

461
00:23:03,440 --> 00:23:05,000
just because Duan Qiyan signed up.

462
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,000
His grades are way better than mine.

463
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,640
Wouldn't it be ridiculous
for someone with my math scores

464
00:23:08,640 --> 00:23:09,970
to enter a math contest?

465
00:23:11,610 --> 00:23:13,010
I've noticed something.

466
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:16,270
You're absolutely
the biggest backtalker in this house.

467
00:23:16,270 --> 00:23:17,070
Every time I say anything,

468
00:23:17,070 --> 00:23:19,070
you've always got a comeback ready.

469
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:20,920
I'm your mother.

470
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,510
Isn't this all for your own good?

471
00:23:22,510 --> 00:23:23,680
Then why is it

472
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:25,030
that other kids have all signed up,

473
00:23:25,030 --> 00:23:26,400
but my kid can't?

474
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:27,960
What other kids?

475
00:23:28,110 --> 00:23:30,440
Isn't it just Lin Zhixia
who has signed up?

476
00:23:30,590 --> 00:23:31,720
She's the top student in the whole school.

477
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:33,400
If she doesn't participate, who will?

478
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:35,000
Hardly anyone
from other classes signed up.

479
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,240
Why do you have to compare yourself
to students from other classes?

480
00:23:37,240 --> 00:23:39,750
Can't you just
compare yourself with Lin Zhixia?

481
00:23:39,750 --> 00:23:41,960
If you must compare me to Lin Zhixia,

482
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:43,270
I've got more friends than she does.

483
00:23:43,270 --> 00:23:44,310
Why don't you compare
that strength of mine to hers?

484
00:23:44,310 --> 00:23:46,700
Does the college entrance exam
test popularity?

485
00:23:46,700 --> 00:23:49,030
C-Can having lots of friends
get you into top universities?

486
00:23:49,030 --> 00:23:49,790
Seriously.

487
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:51,790
Tang Tingting,

488
00:23:51,790 --> 00:23:52,920
I've realized something now.

489
00:23:52,920 --> 00:23:55,780
I-I've realized
your problem isn't your studying.

490
00:23:56,030 --> 00:23:57,880
It's your mindset.

491
00:23:58,070 --> 00:24:00,000
Your attitude is the real problem.

492
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:02,440
Fine then, you don't have to sign up.

493
00:24:02,550 --> 00:24:03,640
Hand over all those

494
00:24:04,030 --> 00:24:05,200
a-albums of yours.

495
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:05,790
Mom!

496
00:24:07,200 --> 00:24:09,070
I already told you
I'm not cut out for this.

497
00:24:09,070 --> 00:24:10,550
Are you seriously
going to force me to join?

498
00:24:10,550 --> 00:24:11,880
Fine, I'll go sign up tomorrow.

499
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:12,920
But if I get eliminated
in the first round,

500
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:14,790
don't complain that I embarrassed you.

501
00:24:14,790 --> 00:24:15,750
I'll be embarrassed?

502
00:24:15,750 --> 00:24:17,590
Who will really be embarrassed?

503
00:24:20,250 --> 00:24:21,070
Where are you going?

504
00:24:21,070 --> 00:24:22,000
To clear my head.

505
00:24:34,880 --> 00:24:35,480
Tingting.

506
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:38,480
Why are you all here?

507
00:24:41,110 --> 00:24:42,680
I was just looking for you.

508
00:24:43,350 --> 00:24:45,070
Looking for me? What for?

509
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:49,360
I'd like to invite you
to join my team for the math contest.

510
00:24:51,480 --> 00:24:52,680
What a coincidence.

511
00:24:53,160 --> 00:24:54,680
I was actually planning to
find two people tomorrow

512
00:24:54,680 --> 00:24:55,790
to sign up with.

513
00:24:59,640 --> 00:25:01,170
But I won't team up with you.

514
00:25:03,510 --> 00:25:04,310
Why?

515
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:08,530
I'm only entering
to get my mom off my back.

516
00:25:08,550 --> 00:25:10,510
I'll be perfectly happy
getting eliminated in the first round.

517
00:25:10,510 --> 00:25:12,310
How could I
drag the top student down with me?

518
00:25:12,310 --> 00:25:13,680
Are you stupid?

519
00:25:14,070 --> 00:25:15,930
This is such a great opportunity.

520
00:25:22,110 --> 00:25:23,480
Let us talk alone.

521
00:25:24,160 --> 00:25:25,720
It's close to my home anyway.

522
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:27,180
You guys should head back.

523
00:25:28,830 --> 00:25:30,680
Alright. We'll head back first.

524
00:25:35,480 --> 00:25:36,610
Aren't you leaving?

525
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:38,200
This is our team's business.

526
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:39,460
Of course I'm staying.

527
00:25:40,160 --> 00:25:40,960
Alright.

528
00:25:41,110 --> 00:25:42,200
Come on. Let's go.

529
00:25:46,030 --> 00:25:47,790
You guys are really something,

530
00:25:47,790 --> 00:25:48,960
asking me to be your teammate.

531
00:25:48,960 --> 00:25:50,400
You really couldn't find anyone else, huh?

532
00:25:50,400 --> 00:25:51,110
Yes.

533
00:25:54,980 --> 00:25:57,070
Registration is closing soon.

534
00:25:57,070 --> 00:25:58,680
Finding two teammates at the last minute

535
00:25:58,680 --> 00:25:59,680
would be hard for you too, right?

536
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:00,830
I'm not aiming for any prizes.

537
00:26:00,830 --> 00:26:02,490
I'll just find any two people.

538
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:06,600
Who's going to join you just to get
knocked out in the first round?

539
00:26:06,880 --> 00:26:09,790
If you pick me,
you'll be eliminated in the first round.

540
00:26:09,790 --> 00:26:10,680
Don't make things harder on yourselves.

541
00:26:10,680 --> 00:26:12,480
You'd better find someone else.

542
00:26:15,550 --> 00:26:17,080
Have you ever thought about

543
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:19,930
getting first place
to get your mom off your back?

544
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,030
Me?

545
00:26:24,110 --> 00:26:25,350
Since you're signing up anyway,

546
00:26:25,350 --> 00:26:26,550
wouldn't it be a shame

547
00:26:26,790 --> 00:26:28,850
to get eliminated in the first round?

548
00:26:30,350 --> 00:26:31,790
So what am I supposed to do?

549
00:26:31,790 --> 00:26:33,310
That's the best I can do.

550
00:26:34,350 --> 00:26:35,880
Of course, you wouldn't pull it off alone.

551
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:37,480
But if you join Lin Zhixia's team,

552
00:26:37,480 --> 00:26:38,240
winning first place

553
00:26:38,240 --> 00:26:39,840
isn't entirely impossible.

554
00:26:41,070 --> 00:26:41,790
Right?

555
00:26:44,830 --> 00:26:45,720
Yes.

556
00:26:47,550 --> 00:26:49,680
There's still some time
before the preliminary round.

557
00:26:49,680 --> 00:26:52,070
I can make
an intensive study plan for you.

558
00:26:52,090 --> 00:26:53,510
An intensive study plan?

559
00:26:54,510 --> 00:26:56,640
Isn't that exactly what broke Duan Qiyan?

560
00:26:56,640 --> 00:26:59,680
Just because he couldn't handle it
doesn't mean you can't.

561
00:26:59,680 --> 00:27:01,200
He likes to have fun,

562
00:27:01,330 --> 00:27:03,200
but his grades are still pretty good.

563
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:04,200
His old nickname

564
00:27:04,230 --> 00:27:06,160
was the "King of
the Affiliated Elementary School."

565
00:27:06,160 --> 00:27:07,830
You earned your place

566
00:27:07,850 --> 00:27:09,400
in the experimental class too.

567
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:10,930
Don't sell yourself short.

568
00:27:16,160 --> 00:27:17,160
Imagine

569
00:27:18,030 --> 00:27:20,160
what will happen if you get first place

570
00:27:20,590 --> 00:27:21,680
in the contest.

571
00:27:24,270 --> 00:27:27,400
If I get first place...

572
00:27:29,640 --> 00:27:32,400
my mom will probably
buy me the latest phone

573
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:35,000
and treat me to a big meal.

574
00:27:35,960 --> 00:27:38,720
Maybe she'll even stop nagging me
about idol-chasing.

575
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:39,750
Leave it to me.

576
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:43,220
I'll do everything I can
to lead the team to first place.

577
00:27:46,720 --> 00:27:47,510
So?

578
00:27:47,830 --> 00:27:50,790
Are you willing to join our team?

579
00:27:52,790 --> 00:27:55,680
You really want me as your teammate?

580
00:27:58,240 --> 00:27:59,920
I was so mean to you before,

581
00:28:00,160 --> 00:28:02,760
and I even gave you
that nickname, "Immortal."

582
00:28:03,130 --> 00:28:04,880
You don't mind?

583
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:08,930
Lots of people call me that.

584
00:28:09,110 --> 00:28:10,030
I'm used to it.

585
00:28:12,960 --> 00:28:14,400
Then let me make one thing clear first.

586
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:15,720
I'm really not good at math.

587
00:28:15,720 --> 00:28:17,310
If I mess up, you can't blame me.

588
00:28:17,310 --> 00:28:18,240
Enough talking.

589
00:28:18,510 --> 00:28:19,440
Since you've joined us,

590
00:28:19,440 --> 00:28:20,440
commit to it.

591
00:28:20,640 --> 00:28:23,240
Aiming for first place
in the entire province.

592
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:24,260
What do you say?

593
00:28:29,350 --> 00:28:30,350
My two teammates?

594
00:28:33,030 --> 00:28:33,920
Deal.

595
00:28:36,030 --> 00:28:36,790
Deal.

596
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:37,960
Deal.

597
00:29:13,480 --> 00:29:15,720
This is a geometric sequence
where we're solving for the common ratio q.

598
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:18,750
So set point B... This point.

599
00:29:20,400 --> 00:29:23,000
Assume point B equals point A...
Write it down.

600
00:29:24,550 --> 00:29:26,590
A1 plus A2 plus A3...

601
00:29:27,440 --> 00:29:28,240
Then...

602
00:29:28,260 --> 00:29:28,980
Stop.

603
00:29:30,030 --> 00:29:31,960
Do you understand it, Shen Fuxuan?

604
00:29:32,270 --> 00:29:33,250
Yeah.

605
00:29:33,510 --> 00:29:34,590
What's so hard to understand?

606
00:29:34,590 --> 00:29:36,070
She's explained it so many times already.

607
00:29:36,070 --> 00:29:37,240
I know.

608
00:29:37,240 --> 00:29:38,900
But I still don't quite get it.

609
00:29:39,030 --> 00:29:41,560
That's okay.
We can go over it a few more times.

610
00:29:43,270 --> 00:29:45,470
How about this? We can study at my place.

611
00:29:45,750 --> 00:29:47,720
We can talk as loudly as we want there.

612
00:29:47,720 --> 00:29:49,450
And maybe when my mom sees

613
00:29:49,480 --> 00:29:50,880
how hard I'm studying,

614
00:29:50,880 --> 00:29:51,640
she'll get so happy

615
00:29:51,640 --> 00:29:54,100
that she'll give me back
my precious albums.

616
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:55,270
Please.

617
00:29:55,270 --> 00:29:57,470
I haven't listened to his songs in ages.

618
00:29:57,880 --> 00:29:59,200
All right. Let's gather our stuff.

619
00:29:59,200 --> 00:29:59,830
Okay.

620
00:30:01,550 --> 00:30:03,270
Then let me finish this problem.
Two minutes.

621
00:30:03,270 --> 00:30:03,850
Okay.

622
00:30:04,590 --> 00:30:05,550
We'll wait for you at the door.

623
00:30:05,550 --> 00:30:06,240
Okay.

624
00:30:14,790 --> 00:30:17,510
Tang Tingting's riding
Lin Zhixia's coattails into the contest—

625
00:30:17,510 --> 00:30:18,640
she's pretty lucky.

626
00:30:20,640 --> 00:30:22,840
Tang Tingting's dead last in the class.

627
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:25,160
Shen Fuxuan is okay, though.

628
00:30:26,310 --> 00:30:27,310
But no matter how strong Lin Zhixia is,

629
00:30:27,310 --> 00:30:29,110
she can't carry a hopeless team.

630
00:30:30,880 --> 00:30:31,960
You have a point.

631
00:30:33,350 --> 00:30:34,680
I should study hard too.

632
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:51,090
Need something?

633
00:30:54,270 --> 00:30:58,130
Sounds like you all have some
strong opinions about what makes a team.

634
00:30:58,440 --> 00:30:59,700
I'd really like to know

635
00:31:00,310 --> 00:31:02,240
what kind of results a deserter...

636
00:31:02,830 --> 00:31:04,290
a perennial runner-up...

637
00:31:06,640 --> 00:31:08,270
and a measly seventh place

638
00:31:09,510 --> 00:31:11,310
can possibly achieve together.

639
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:21,110
Jeez.

640
00:31:22,750 --> 00:31:24,640
Aren't our grudges settled?

641
00:31:24,640 --> 00:31:26,370
Why does he still talk that way?

642
00:31:26,880 --> 00:31:28,140
That guy, Shen Fuxuan,

643
00:31:28,240 --> 00:31:29,590
has such a sharp tongue,

644
00:31:29,590 --> 00:31:31,190
he might cut himself with it.

645
00:31:34,720 --> 00:31:38,380
Lin Zhixia, how are you still studying
while just standing there?

646
00:31:38,830 --> 00:31:41,650
There's actually a much simpler way
to solve this problem.

647
00:31:41,650 --> 00:31:42,310
Hold on.

648
00:31:42,510 --> 00:31:44,440
Let me take a break. I'm exhausted.

649
00:31:44,590 --> 00:31:45,920
Then look at it again
when we get to your place.

650
00:31:45,920 --> 00:31:47,110
I'm going to find Jiang Yubai.

651
00:31:47,110 --> 00:31:48,970
He asked me about it during class.

652
00:31:49,160 --> 00:31:51,880
Lin Zhixia, they're our competitors.

653
00:31:52,750 --> 00:31:53,590
I know.

654
00:31:53,750 --> 00:31:55,640
But Jiang Yubai is also my good friend.

655
00:31:55,640 --> 00:31:56,400
Don't worry.

656
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:57,160
They won't use

657
00:31:57,160 --> 00:32:00,020
the exact same problems
during the actual contest.

658
00:32:02,960 --> 00:32:03,750
Jiang Yubai,

659
00:32:04,480 --> 00:32:06,610
you saw how Shen Fuxuan acted just now.

660
00:32:06,790 --> 00:32:08,520
Do you know where you stand now?

661
00:32:11,350 --> 00:32:12,410
I've always known.

662
00:32:13,510 --> 00:32:14,070
Good.

663
00:32:14,550 --> 00:32:15,720
Then our team's goal

664
00:32:15,920 --> 00:32:17,250
is to defeat Lin Zhixia.

665
00:32:17,830 --> 00:32:21,830
And I want to beat them so thoroughly
they have no choice but to accept it.

666
00:32:22,160 --> 00:32:23,020
Same goal here.

667
00:32:24,030 --> 00:32:26,440
I feel like you two are fired up now.

668
00:32:26,440 --> 00:32:27,640
So motivated.

669
00:32:29,550 --> 00:32:30,150
Oh, right.

670
00:32:30,270 --> 00:32:31,030
Jiang Yubai,

671
00:32:31,590 --> 00:32:33,320
you and Lin Zhixia are so close.

672
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:34,480
If

673
00:32:34,480 --> 00:32:35,830
we beat them,

674
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:38,060
what will happen to your friendship?

675
00:32:40,590 --> 00:32:42,720
I've always wanted to beat Lin Zhixia.

676
00:32:43,880 --> 00:32:46,420
This contest is our best chance.

677
00:32:47,880 --> 00:32:49,610
Right now, I don't see a friend—

678
00:32:49,750 --> 00:32:50,590
I see my rival.

679
00:33:12,350 --> 00:33:14,480
I've always wanted to beat Lin Zhixia.

680
00:33:15,070 --> 00:33:17,440
This contest is our best chance.

681
00:33:18,070 --> 00:33:19,800
Right now, I don't see a friend—

682
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:20,880
I see my rival.

683
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:08,940
Lin Zhixia.

684
00:34:09,920 --> 00:34:10,480
Morning.

685
00:34:11,070 --> 00:34:11,760
Morning.

686
00:34:18,460 --> 00:34:20,989
Let's look at
this original contest problem.

687
00:34:21,570 --> 00:34:22,920
An insulated container is divided

688
00:34:22,920 --> 00:34:25,280
by a partition
into a gas chamber and a vacuum.

689
00:34:25,280 --> 00:34:27,070
The partition is removed,
allowing the gas to expand freely.

690
00:34:27,070 --> 00:34:29,880
Lin Zhixia, could you explain

691
00:34:29,920 --> 00:34:32,050
the problem the teacher just covered?

692
00:34:32,590 --> 00:34:33,400
Sorry.

693
00:34:33,710 --> 00:34:36,170
I wasn't listening to
what the teacher was saying.

694
00:34:36,170 --> 00:34:38,770
As the molecules spread farther apart,
their potential energy increases,

695
00:34:38,770 --> 00:34:40,010
their kinetic energy decreases,

696
00:34:40,010 --> 00:34:41,540
and the temperature drops.

697
00:34:42,010 --> 00:34:44,780
Don't simply apply the ideal gas model
from the textbook.

698
00:34:44,780 --> 00:34:45,670
This is a key testing point.

699
00:34:45,670 --> 00:34:46,800
Pay attention to it.

700
00:34:59,150 --> 00:35:00,510
Free activity time's over.

701
00:35:00,510 --> 00:35:01,840
Everyone, gather here.

702
00:35:08,710 --> 00:35:10,110
Before class ends today,

703
00:35:10,280 --> 00:35:12,960
let's have a fun team obstacle course—

704
00:35:13,230 --> 00:35:14,560
the three-legged race.

705
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:17,590
It'll help develop your coordination

706
00:35:17,590 --> 00:35:18,670
and teamwork.

707
00:35:18,710 --> 00:35:20,590
Now pair up freely.

708
00:35:20,960 --> 00:35:22,110
Find yourselves a partner.

709
00:35:22,110 --> 00:35:24,320
But I must emphasize one rule:

710
00:35:24,510 --> 00:35:26,800
each team must consist of

711
00:35:26,800 --> 00:35:28,070
one boy and one girl.

712
00:35:30,920 --> 00:35:31,510
Okay.

713
00:35:31,670 --> 00:35:32,930
Go find your partners.

714
00:35:34,440 --> 00:35:35,440
Who should we ask?

715
00:35:43,710 --> 00:35:46,150
Lin Zhixia, let's team up.

716
00:35:47,230 --> 00:35:47,920
Okay.

717
00:35:50,030 --> 00:35:50,800
I...

718
00:35:51,230 --> 00:35:52,030
Jiang Yubai.

719
00:35:53,960 --> 00:35:54,840
Let's team up.

720
00:35:55,230 --> 00:35:55,760
Let's go.

721
00:35:59,420 --> 00:36:00,940
Let's pair up.

722
00:36:01,300 --> 00:36:02,160
Let's go, Chun.

723
00:36:03,900 --> 00:36:05,230
Aren't I your teammate?

724
00:36:06,050 --> 00:36:07,650
Am I invisible or something?

725
00:36:15,400 --> 00:36:16,600
Wanna team up with me?

726
00:37:36,170 --> 00:37:36,820
Water.

727
00:37:45,650 --> 00:37:46,450
What's wrong?

728
00:37:47,940 --> 00:37:49,800
You seem to have a lot on your mind.

729
00:37:55,150 --> 00:37:56,610
I heard you said yesterday

730
00:37:56,990 --> 00:37:58,170
that from now on,

731
00:37:58,170 --> 00:38:00,170
we're only opponents, not friends.

732
00:38:00,610 --> 00:38:02,010
Because of this contest,

733
00:38:02,340 --> 00:38:04,140
are we not even friends anymore?

734
00:38:11,760 --> 00:38:14,160
Actually, before we formed teams that day,

735
00:38:14,310 --> 00:38:15,500
Mr. Kong told me

736
00:38:16,300 --> 00:38:19,650
that you already have what it takes
to skip ahead and go to university early,

737
00:38:19,650 --> 00:38:20,980
but I don't.

738
00:38:23,050 --> 00:38:25,380
Those words really struck a chord with me.

739
00:38:27,470 --> 00:38:28,530
This contest

740
00:38:29,170 --> 00:38:31,370
is a great opportunity to prove myself.

741
00:38:31,500 --> 00:38:33,610
That's why, when we were choosing teams,

742
00:38:33,610 --> 00:38:36,140
I deliberately avoided
partnering with you.

743
00:38:38,660 --> 00:38:40,420
I want to give it everything I've got

744
00:38:40,420 --> 00:38:41,820
and compete against you

745
00:38:41,900 --> 00:38:43,760
without any distractions.

746
00:38:44,690 --> 00:38:47,010
I also want to see,
after working so hard for so long,

747
00:38:47,010 --> 00:38:49,270
just how big
the gap between us really is.

748
00:38:50,100 --> 00:38:53,170
Is this contest
really that important to you?

749
00:38:53,970 --> 00:38:54,690
Yes.

750
00:38:56,330 --> 00:38:57,260
Very important.

751
00:39:01,800 --> 00:39:03,400
This was yet another setback

752
00:39:03,780 --> 00:39:05,130
in my social life.

753
00:39:07,390 --> 00:39:09,190
I suddenly find myself doubting

754
00:39:10,070 --> 00:39:13,200
whether all those promises
we made to work hard together

755
00:39:13,230 --> 00:39:15,030
were just my personal illusion.

756
00:39:16,820 --> 00:39:19,420
It turns out Jiang Yubai's true pride

757
00:39:20,590 --> 00:39:22,990
lies in having a rival
worthy of defeating.

758
00:39:24,530 --> 00:39:25,420
And "friend"

759
00:39:27,230 --> 00:39:29,380
was nothing more than a label
I gave myself out of wishful thinking.
